# Line endings.
#
# Most of us are on Windows, but everything runs inside a Linux container. A
# shell script checked out with CRLF line endings fails there with
#   bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M: no such file or directory
# and CRLF in the track .csv files breaks the C++ map parser. So: store and
# check out every text file with LF, on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files that must be LF.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
tools/bri text eol=lf

# Binary: never apply line-ending or text conversion.
*.foxe  binary
*.stl   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pt    binary
*.onnx  binary
*.db3   binary
*.mcap  binary
